    ├── Used APIs  : monkey_patch
    ├── Pitfalls   : gevent.monkey.patch_all() must be called before other imports, same as eventlet; eventlet uses green threads with
    │   implicit yielding; gevent uses explicit hub switching — subtle timing differences may appear; Socket.IO async_mode='gevent' 
    │   requires python-socketio extra; gevent does not patch threading.Thread by default (use patch_all(thread=True))
    └── eventlet.monkey_patch() is called to patch stdlib for cooperative concurrency before importing the Socket.IO app. gevent 
        provides the same monkey-patching capability and is a supported async_mode for python-socketio, making it a genuine drop-in 
        alternative for this specific usage pattern.

