    ├── Pitfalls   : PyCrypto's AES.new accepts key/IV as str/bytes; cryptography requires bytes only; cryptography uses explicit 
    │   padding (e.g., PKCS7) via separate padding module, not null-byte padding; cryptography's API is lower-level: Cipher(algorithm,
    │   mode).encryptor() vs AES.new(key, mode, iv); pycryptodome is a near drop-in replacement (same import path), but still inherits
    │   some PyCrypto quirks; Fixed IV (b'0000000000000000') is a security anti-pattern — should be random per encryption
    ├── Constraints: crypto_required, requires_connector
    └── The code uses PyCrypto's AES in CBC mode with a fixed IV and null-byte padding. Both 'cryptography' (via 
        hazmat.primitives.ciphers) and 'pycryptodome' (drop-in replacement for PyCrypto) provide equivalent AES-CBC functionality. 
        PyCrypto is unmaintained and has known HIGH-severity CVEs (GHSA-6528-wvf6-f6qg, GHSA-cq27-v7xp-c356), so migration is strongly
        recommended.

